description: Security defaults for Octagen public site and future custom CMS
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security baseline

- Never hardcode API keys, tokens, SMTP credentials, or secrets in source files.
- Commit only `.env.example`, never real `.env`.
- Validate external input with schemas before processing or persistence.
- Sanitize HTML or rich text before rendering user-controlled content.
- Add rate limiting and abuse protection for inquiry/contact endpoints.
- Keep admin/auth flows server-side and least-privilege by default.
- Prefer well-maintained dependencies and avoid unnecessary packages.
- Use secure headers and HTTPS assumptions for deployed environments.
